<title>GERMANY: Duerr '96 sales up, dividend unchanged.</title>
<headline>Duerr '96 sales up, dividend unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales			    1,680	 vs 1,471</p>
<p>    Group incoming orders		1,786	 vs 1,610</p>
<p>    Group order book		     1,385	 vs 1,256</p>
<p>    Dividend				  1.20	 vs 1.20 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German plant manufacturing group is Duerr AG.</p>
<p>Dividend payment of 1.20 marks was &quot;possible&quot;, according to a regulatory news release. Group return on sales fell to two percent in 1996 from three percent.</p>
<p>Management said it expected turnover at least unchanged for the current year, while incoming orders could also be kept flat. The company said it was optimistic on profits.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
